.TH TARSH 1 "2026" "tarsh 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tarsh \- a beginner-friendly shell with fzf pickers, fish-style editing and a Python-like script language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tarsh
.RB [ \-l ]
.RB [ \-\-private ]
.br
.B tarsh
.I script
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B tarsh \-c
.I command
.RI [ name " [" args ...]]
.br
.B tarsh \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tarsh
is an interactive shell for Linux. It runs commands, pipes, redirections,
.BR && / || ,
wildcards,
.B $(...)
substitution and job control itself. Lines written for
.BR bash ,
.B zsh
or
.B fish
are recognised, run in that shell, and followed by a one-line note saying what they did.
.PP
Files ending in
.B .tsh
(and lines typed at the prompt) can use
.IR "tarsh script" ,
a small Python-like language in which every line that isn't a statement is a command.
See
.I SCRIPTING.md
in the documentation folder.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c " " \fIcommand\fR
Run one command line and exit. Extra arguments become $0, $1, ...
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-login
Act as a login shell: read
.I /etc/profile
and
.I ~/.profile
(through sh) before starting.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-private
Don't read or save command history.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH INTERACTIVE USE
.TP
.BR cd ", " nvim ", " cp ", " mv ", " rm " followed by space"
Open an fzf picker for a folder or files (needs
.BR fzf ).
.TP
.B Tab
Complete commands, paths, and options (with their descriptions).
.TP
.B Right arrow
Accept the grey suggestion taken from history.
.TP
.B Up arrow
Previous commands; with text typed, previous commands containing it.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Search history.
.TP
.B Alt+Left, Alt+Right
Previous / next folder (on an empty line).
.TP
.B Alt+.
Insert the last argument of the previous command.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z, fg, bg, jobs
Pause programs and bring them back.
.SH HINTS AND LIVE PREVIEW
While a line with
.BR | ,
.BR > ,
.B >>
or
.B <<
is typed, a line under the prompt explains each step and the output to expect.
When every command is listed in
.BR LIVE_COMMANDS ,
the line is also run in a sandbox (no writing, deleting or renaming files, no network,
no signals to other programs, stopped after one second) and the first lines of its output
are shown, with grep matches highlighted.
Writes are simulated: for
.BR "> file" ,
.BR "sed \-i" ,
.B sort \-o
or
.B find \-delete
the preview shows what would be written or deleted.
.B explain
.I line
prints the full breakdown;
.B live
and
.B hints
turn them on or off.
.SH BUILTINS
.BR cd ", " pwd ", " echo ", " export ", " unset ", " set ", " alias ", " unalias ", " abbr ,
.BR source ", " type ", " read ", " shift ", " umask ", " exec ", " true ", " false ,
.BR jobs ", " fg ", " bg ", " wait ", " kill ,
.BR string ", " math ", " count ", " contains ", " random ,
.BR functions ", " funcsave ", " funced ,
.BR prevd ", " nextd ", " dirh ", " cdh ,
.BR history ", " lang ", " explain ", " live ", " hints ", " theme ", " config ", " import\-rc ", " doctor ", " help ", " exit .
.PP
Type
.B help
inside tarsh for a summary of each.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tarsh/tarshrc
Commands run when an interactive tarsh starts: aliases, abbreviations, variables. Edit with
.BR config .
.TP
.I ~/.config/tarsh/config.t
Settings: prompt format, fzf pickers, highlighting, suggestions, explanations, greeting. Edit with
.BR "config settings" .
.TP
.I ~/.config/tarsh/theme.t
The prompt theme. Design it with
.BR "theme edit" ,
or set
.B STARSHIP=on
in config.t to use the starship prompt
.RB ( "theme starship"
for this session).
.TP
.I ~/.config/tarsh/history
Command history.
.TP
.I ~/.config/tarsh/universal
Universal variables
.RB ( "set \-U" ).
.TP
.I ~/.config/tarsh/functions/
Saved functions
.RB ( funcsave ),
loaded on first use.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The status of the last command; 127 for a command that wasn't found, 126 for one that couldn't run,
128+n for one stopped by signal n.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR fish (1),
.BR zsh (1),
.BR fzf (1)
.PP
The guides installed with tarsh:
.IR GUIDE.md ,
.IR SCRIPTING.md ,
.IR INSTALL.md .
